h","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":3},{"base":"H5813","lemma":"עֻזִּי","tr":"uz·zi","gloss":"Uzzi","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H8435","lemma":"תּוֹלֵדוֹת","tr":"to·le·dah","gloss":"generation","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":39},{"base":"H3485","lemma":"יִשָּׂשכָר","tr":"yis·sa·s·khar","gloss":"Issachar","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":43},{"base":"H0505","lemma":"אֶ֫לֶף","tr":"e·leph","gloss":"thousand","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":506},{"base":"H1368","lemma":"גִּבּוֹר","tr":"gib·bor","gloss":"mighty man","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":159},{"base":"H8337","lemma":"שֵׁשׁ","tr":"shesh","gloss":"six","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":216},{"base":"H2428","lemma":"חַ֫יִל","tr":"cha·yil","gloss":"strength: soldiers","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":246},{"base":"H3437","lemma":"יָשׁוּב","tr":"ya·shuv","gloss":"Jashub","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The sons of Issachar: Tola, Puvah, Job, and Shimron.","from":1},{"book":"NUM","chapter":26,"verse":23,"verseEnd":24,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"These were the descendants of Issachar by their clans: The Tolaite clan from Tola, the Punite clan from Puvah, the Jashubite clan from Jashub, and the Shimronite clan from Shimron.","from":1},{"book":"2SA","chapter":24,"verse":1,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Again the anger of the LORD burned against Israel, and He stirred up David against them, saying, “Go and take a census of Israel and Judah.” So the king said to Joab the commander of his army, who was with him, “Go now throughout the tribes of Israel from Dan to Beersheba and register the troops, so that I may know their number.” But Joab replied to the king, “May the LORD your God multiply the troops a hundred times over, and may the eyes of my lord the king see it. But why does my lord the king want to do such a thing?” Nevertheless, the kingʼs word prevailed against Joab and against the commanders of the army. So Joab and the commanders of the army departed from the presence of the king to register the troops of Israel. They crossed the Jordan and camped near Aroer, south of the town in the middle of the valley, and proceeded toward Gad and Jazer.","from":2},{"book":"1CH","chapter":12,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"From Issachar, men who understood the times and knew what Israel should do: 200 chiefs with all their kinsmen at their command.","from":4},{"book":"1CH","chapter":21,"verse":1,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Satan rose up against Israel and incited David to take a census of Israel. So David said to Joab and the commanders of the troops, “Go and count the Israelites from Beersheba to Dan and bring me a report, so that I may know their number.” But Joab replied, “May the LORD multiply His troops a hundred times over. My lord the king, are they not all servants of my lord? Why does my lord want to do this? Why should he bring guilt on Israel?” Nevertheless, the kingʼs word prevailed against Joab. So Joab departed and traveled throughout Israel, and then he returned to Jerusalem. And Joab reported to David the total number of the troops. In all Israel there were 1,100,000 men who drew the sword, including 470,000 in Judah.","from":2},{"book":"1CH","chapter":27,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"This is the list of the Israelites—the heads of families, the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and their officers who served the king in every matter concerning the divisions on rotating military duty each month throughout the year. There were 24,000 men in each division:","from":2},{"book":"1CH","chapter":27,"verse":23,"verseEnd":24,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"David did not count the men aged twenty or under, because the LORD had said that He would make Israel as numerous as the stars of the sky. Joab son of Zeruiah began to count the men but did not finish. For because of this census wrath came upon Israel, and the number was not entered in the Book of the Chronicles of King David.","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"6-12":{"people":[{"id":"jediael-h3043g","name":"Jediael","kind":"person","brief":"Benjamin leader","count":3,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"becher-h1071g","name":"Becher","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Benjamin","count":2,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"bela-h1106a","name":"Bela","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Benjamin and father of Ezbon","count":2,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"benjamin-h1144g","name":"Benjamin","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"ezbon-h0675h","name":"Ezbon","kind":"person","brief":"Benjamin warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"iri-h5901","name":"Iri","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Bela","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"jerimoth-h3406g","name":"Jerimoth","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Bela","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"uzzi-h5813i","name":"Uzzi","kind":"person","brief":"Benjamite warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"uzziel-h5816i","name":"Uzziel","kind":"person","brief":"Benjamite warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"abijah-h0029k","name":"Abijah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Becher","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"alemeth-h5964h","name":"Alemeth","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Becher","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"anathoth-h6068h","name":"Anathoth","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Becher","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"eliezer-h0461i","name":"Eliezer","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Becher","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"elioenai-h0454i","name":"Elioenai","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Becher","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"jeremoth-h3406h","name":"Jeremoth","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Becher","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"joash-h3135g","name":"Joash","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Becher","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"omri-h6018h","name":"Omri","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Becher","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"zemir