:"Bezer","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Zophah","count":1,"firstVerse":37},{"id":"hod-h1936","name":"Hod","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Zophah","count":1,"firstVerse":37},{"id":"shamma-h8037h","name":"Shamma","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Zophah","count":1,"firstVerse":37},{"id":"shilshah-h8030","name":"Shilshah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Zophah","count":1,"firstVerse":37},{"id":"ara-h0690","name":"Ara","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Ithran","count":1,"firstVerse":38},{"id":"jephunneh-h3312h","name":"Jephunneh","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Ithran","count":1,"firstVerse":38},{"id":"pispa-h6462","name":"Pispa","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Ithran","count":1,"firstVerse":38},{"id":"arah-h0733g","name":"Arah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shual","count":1,"firstVerse":39},{"id":"hanniel-h2592h","name":"Hanniel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shual","count":1,"firstVerse":39},{"id":"rizia-h7525","name":"Rizia","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Shual","count":1,"firstVerse":39}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3310","lemma":"יַפְלֵט","tr":"yaph·let","gloss":"Japhlet","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":3},{"base":"H6690","lemma":"צוֹפַח","tr":"tso·phach","gloss":"Zophah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H1283","lemma":"בְּרִיעָה","tr":"be·ri·ah","gloss":"Beriah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H2268","lemma":"חֶ֫בֶר","tr":"che·ver","gloss":"Heber","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H0836","lemma":"אָשֵׁר","tr":"a·sher","gloss":"Asher","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":43},{"base":"H0269","lemma":"אָחוֹת","tr":"a·chot","gloss":"sister","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":114},{"base":"H0277","lemma":"אֲחִי","tr":"a·chi","gloss":"Ahi","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H2369","lemma":"חוֹתָם","tr":"cho·tam","gloss":"Hotham","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H2592","lemma":"חַנִּיאֵל","tr":"chan·ni·el","gloss":"Hanniel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3438","lemma":"יִשְׁוָה","tr":"yish·vah","gloss":"Ishvah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The children of Asher: Imnah, Ishvah, Ishvi, Beriah, and their sister Serah. The sons of Beriah: Heber and Malchiel.","from":30},{"book":"NUM","chapter":26,"verse":44,"verseEnd":46,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"These were the descendants of Asher by their clans: The Imnite clan from Imnah, the Ishvite clan from Ishvi, and the Beriite clan from Beriah. And these were the descendants of Beriah: the Heberite clan from Heber and the Malchielite clan from Malchiel. And the name of Asherʼs daughter was Serah.","from":30},{"book":"2SA","chapter":24,"verse":1,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Again the anger of the LORD burned against Israel, and He stirred up David against them, saying, “Go and take a census of Israel and Judah.” So the king said to Joab the commander of his army, who was with him, “Go now throughout the tribes of Israel from Dan to Beersheba and register the troops, so that I may know their number.” But Joab replied to the king, “May the LORD your God multiply the troops a hundred times over, and may the eyes of my lord the king see it. But why does my lord the king want to do such a thing?” Nevertheless, the kingʼs word prevailed against Joab and against the commanders of the army. So Joab and the commanders of the army departed from the presence of the king to register the troops of Israel. They crossed the Jordan and camped near Aroer, south of the town in the middle of the valley, and proceeded toward Gad and Jazer.","from":40},{"book":"1CH","chapter":21,"verse":1,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Satan rose up against Israel and incited David to take a census of Israel. So David said to Joab and the commanders of the troops, “Go and count the Israelites from Beersheba to Dan and bring me a report, so that I may know their number.” But Joab replied, “May the LORD multiply His troops a hundred times over. My lord the king, are they not all servants of my lord? Why does my lord want to do this? Why should he bring guilt on Israel?” Nevertheless, the kingʼs word prevailed against Joab. So Joab departed and traveled throughout Israel, and then he returned to Jerusalem. And Joab reported to David the total number of the troops. In all Israel there were 1,100,000 men who drew the sword, including 470,000 in Judah.","from":40}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}